WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.358 --> 00:00:01.191
(audience applauds)

00:00:01.191 --> 00:00:02.680
- Oh my gosh, everybody
looks so cute today.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.110
Look at those boots, what?

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.800
- [Maggie] Wow, thank
you, I brought you roses.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.633
- [Kelly] You did?

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:07.466
- I brought you roses, no, these.

00:00:07.466 --> 00:00:08.309
- I like it, I know.

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:09.470
You'd say that's so beautiful.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.303
- This is a great couch,

00:00:10.303 --> 00:00:12.420
I'm honored to be in between you two.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.253
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:00:13.253 --> 00:00:14.581
No, I'm excited to have you on the show.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.414
(audience applauds)

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:16.247
Thank you so much for taking the time.

00:00:16.247 --> 00:00:17.080
- Thanks for having
me, it's my first time.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.760
- So wait, is it true that
you fought through a fever,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.380
in a very important audition?

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.240
- Yeah, I mean, my first U.S. movie

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.700
was "Mission Impossible Three".

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.760
And I flew here from Asia and...

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.310
- That was your first movie?

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.469
- That's what Tom cruise said.

00:00:31.469 --> 00:00:33.309
(audience and Maggie laugh)

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:35.130
- I was like, "Geez, what?"

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.980
- I got here and then the jet lag sort of,

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.370
hits you at about 3:30,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.880
when you fly from that side of the world.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.450
I was living on that side
of the world at the time.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.850
And so, of course they
called me in the morning

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.010
and said, "Your audition's at 3:30".

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.830
I'm like, "Oh no, oh God".

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.000
And then when I woke up,
I had a raging fever.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.460
And then so, I sort of went to Paramount

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.470
and this casting director,
who I'll never forget

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.070
was so kind to me and just sort of,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.430
like said, "Maggie, I
need you to be normal

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.460
for 10 minutes".

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.293
- [Kelly] Normal.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.338
- You know, just 10 minutes
and your life will be changed.

00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:04.171
- Yeah.

00:01:04.171 --> 00:01:05.670
- But I went from, I mean,
I was shaking like this.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.070
I was like, and my tea
was spilling all over me

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.220
and then I got hot and sweaty.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.130
And so, this was happening
throughout the audition,

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.260
but I just sort of,
sucked it up and I did it

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.995
and the rest is history.

00:01:16.995 --> 00:01:18.968
- [Kelly] Wow, congratulations,
"Mission Impossible".

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:19.801
(Maggie and audience laugh)
- Thank you.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:20.950
- [Kelly] I was like, "That's amazing".

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.140
- [Maggie] Sometimes
you have to suck it up.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:22.973
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:22.973 --> 00:01:23.935
- [Maggie] Yeah.

00:01:23.935 --> 00:01:24.770
No one cares how you're feeling, right?

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.603
- No, no one cares.

00:01:25.603 --> 00:01:26.870
- You know this, you're
on camera all the time.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.170
You can't have a bad day.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.168
I mean, no one cares, no
one's going to be like...

00:01:29.168 --> 00:01:30.001
- [Kelly] Well in their defense...

00:01:30.001 --> 00:01:31.310
- "You know, Katie
Couric's having a bad day

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.143
that's why she..."

00:01:32.143 --> 00:01:34.210
- Yeah well, and they do
that like in shows too.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.920
Like, I was so bad because it's like,

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.370
you try and give your
best because it's like,

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:38.870
this is their one time to see you.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.520
Like, that's why yeah,
you try, sometimes...

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.203
- And it's, the only
impression you're going to get.

00:01:42.203 --> 00:01:44.580
It was either like, she was forgettable

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.396
or like, maybe there's something here.

00:01:46.396 --> 00:01:47.780
(Kelly and Maggie laugh)

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.730
- [Kelly] So, it's so in concrete.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:49.960
Oh my God. I'm stressed out.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.770
Oh wait, so your new
show is called "Pivoting.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:52.603
- [Maggie] Yes.

00:01:52.603 --> 00:01:54.040
- So, tell us about it and
tell us about your character.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.010
- I'm so excited because
I'm doing a comedy,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.700
which is so fun and just, I've never,

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.030
no one's ever cast me in a comedy.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.160
I mean, I did movies where I
had comedic elements in them,

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.940
but never really trusted
me to like lead a project,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:06.773
with other funny women.

00:02:06.773 --> 00:02:07.606
- That's exciting for an actor

00:02:07.606 --> 00:02:08.930
to get to do like different things, yeah.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.720
- I go to work, I laugh all day,

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.440
I love my co-stars, I love our
writers, I love our creator.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.440
We just, we have such
a good time together.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.273
And then I go home,

00:02:16.273 --> 00:02:17.840
because I've done action
movies, my whole life.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.890
And I feel like, that's pretty much

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:20.950
the relationship right there.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.578
That look on my face.
- I love the chic moment.

00:02:22.578 --> 00:02:23.957
- Yeah.
(Maggie laughs)

00:02:23.957 --> 00:02:25.950
I go home and I feel
like I didn't even work,

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.740
because normally I'm like sore or...

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.573
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:29.573 --> 00:02:30.484
- You know, I mean, I have to have

00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:31.930
some kind of like ailment,
because of the action I'm doing.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:32.763
- [Kelly] You've got beaten up.

00:02:32.763 --> 00:02:33.596
- I've gotten beaten up.

00:02:33.596 --> 00:02:35.810
- Is there anything like, because
of the title of your show,

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.740
is there anywhere you feel like you,

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.120
maybe should have pivoted
in life or you did pivot?

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.670
That was like, really good.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.503
- Oh gosh.

00:02:42.503 --> 00:02:44.030
Now, I don't have an
addiction to shopping,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.180
it's not an addiction.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.260
- Now when you lead with that,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.336
you might have a problem.

00:02:48.336 --> 00:02:49.469
(Maggie laughs)

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.440
When you lead with, I
don't have a problem, but.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.029
- Yeah, she doubts the
protest too much, yeah.

00:02:53.029 --> 00:02:53.862
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:53.862 --> 00:02:55.240
So, I just sort of,

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.263
you know, you notice
when the boxes arrive.

00:02:57.263 --> 00:02:58.096
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:02:58.096 --> 00:02:59.570
- [Maggie] And you just go,
"Well, that's interesting".

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.710
Because I'm having boxes arrive more times

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:02.624
than I should, right?

00:03:02.624 --> 00:03:04.660
But it, it's too much of it.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.357
And I kind of realized I just went,

00:03:06.357 --> 00:03:07.500
"Well, something's wrong with me".

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.840
Obviously, something's wrong with me.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.950
So I said, "I'm going to
stop this for a month".

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:11.820
A month, I'm just going to,

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.430
I'm going to see cute
stuff and I don't want it.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.300
I'm just not going to do it.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.250
And then I failed, last
week and I bought one thing

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.340
and now I have to start
over because I'm not a liar.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.173
I don't lie.

00:03:21.173 --> 00:03:22.160
Like, if I have a goal.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.270
- Okay, yeah.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.280
- And I don't meet it, I'll start over.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.537
I'm not going to pretend it
didn't happen, it happened.

00:03:25.537 --> 00:03:26.370
- [Kelly] Oh, I can't do that either.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.522
- I failed.

00:03:27.522 --> 00:03:28.355
- [Kelly] Because that's
not winning, yeah.

00:03:28.355 --> 00:03:29.188
- No, that's not winning, yeah.

00:03:29.188 --> 00:03:30.740
And you can't lie to yourself.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.573
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:31.573 --> 00:03:33.278
- Thoughts watching, whatever.

00:03:33.278 --> 00:03:35.360
- But I think it's really easy,
when you're shopping online,

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.781
I notice that I accidentally...

00:03:36.781 --> 00:03:37.740
- [Kelly] It's a click away.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:38.884
- Get two of everything.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:39.861
- [Maggie] Me too, accidentally.

00:03:39.861 --> 00:03:41.422
- How does this happen?

00:03:41.422 --> 00:03:42.553
(audience laughs)

00:03:42.553 --> 00:03:44.782
It literally just happened to me.

00:03:44.782 --> 00:03:46.284
- What didn't I check on this form that,

00:03:46.284 --> 00:03:48.084
you know it's terrible.

00:03:48.084 --> 00:03:49.153
- [Maggie] There's no consequence either.

00:03:49.153 --> 00:03:51.534
- This happens all the
time, the quantity thing.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:52.367
- [Maggie] The quantity thing.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.200
- The quantity thing.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.070
I'm like, "I didn't order two tea makers,

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.000
Why do I need two tea
makers? Why would I do that?"

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.982
- They don't want you to
send it back, it's a scam.

00:03:57.982 --> 00:03:58.930
- [Katie] I don't even know I ordered two,

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.367
until they arrive and I'm like,

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:01.200
"How come I have two of them?"

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.060
- You know what? They get me too.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.060
Because when I do the quantity thing,

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.480
then I end up giving it to someone,

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:05.313
I'm just like, "Here, I just got extra".

00:04:05.313 --> 00:04:08.470
- It happened to me last week
with salt and pepper shakers.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.454
I got two and I went, "Here you go, Mom".

00:04:10.454 --> 00:04:12.402
- That happened to me with
my Lululemon tennis skirt.

00:04:12.402 --> 00:04:13.774
(Katie and audience laugh)

00:04:13.774 --> 00:04:15.510
- [Kelly] We are the
suckers, we are suckers.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.850
We're falling for it.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:17.683
- We are.

00:04:17.683 --> 00:04:18.730
- [Kelly] I know, I know,

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:19.767
- Dammit.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:20.730
- All right, everybody time
for another quick break.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.380
But Maggie's show is called "Pivoting",

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.240
you have to watch it.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.410
It's Thursdays on Fox.
(audience applauds)

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.040
We should also mention Maggie has a line

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.710
of environmentally-friendly,
athletic wear,

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.093
which I'm very into, called, Qeep Up.

00:04:32.093 --> 00:04:33.160
Qeep Up, with a Q,

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.110
because Maggie Q because she's adorable

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:36.130
and it's an awesome idea.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.430
I thought that was so cute.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.070
You can look for it online, everybody

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.916
and buy doubles, everybody does.

00:04:40.916 --> 00:04:42.479
(Kelly laughs)

